and not the `publish` call itself.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1496994449,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwNzMyMDQ1Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1548#issuecomment-307320453"},"message":"I think I found the issue.\nThe setup doesn't use `datalad install` for creating `origin`. This leads to `origin` having a `.git` symlink instead of directory, while `source` has its own `.git` dir. If you adapt origin accordingly, the push works just fine.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1496994697,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwNzMyMTI2OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1548#issuecomment-307321268"},"message":"We need to use `datalad` for creating those testrepos or have a (plumbing?) command to fix up hierarchies with symlinked .git","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1496994763,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwNzMyMTQ2OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1548#issuecomment-307321468"},"message":"Thanks!\n\nNow the question is: how do we adjust? The way you suggest will fix the issue for ourselves, but it is (and should be) absolutely possible that people use datalad with non-datalad repos.\n\nIn general I think the testrepos setup is not good. We are not testing on what we would be producing in real life.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1496995096,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwNzMyMjU3Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1548#issuecomment-307322576"},"message":"Well, it's about being able to publish to a non-datalad repo. How about letting `configure-sibling` do the fix? It wouldn't convert it to an actual datalad repo, but just replace those symlinks. (No .datalad creation or sth)","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1496997341,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MTExNjg1NTMyMA=="},"added":[],"removed":["on hold - input required"]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1496997341,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MTExNjg1NTMyMQ=="},"added":[],"removed":["question"]},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1496997364,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50MTExNjg1NTgzMg=="},"title":"Testrepo setup causes `git push` to fail","was":"datalad search blows hard"},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1496997371,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDExMTY4NTU5NjU="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1497000976,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwNzM0Mzc3OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1548#issuecomment-307343778"},"message":"BTW: I wonder whether we should ask git folks whether this is considered to be a bug. If .git is allowed to be a symlink as well as a directory, this should not prevent pushing, I think.","files":null}]}